<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Mud Puddle</h1>
<p>Sphere: Creation Sphere
Class: Druid (guild level 8)
Mana: 15
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast mud puddle
</pre>
<p>The caster calls upon the waters to soak the ground, and water wells up 
from below into a slick puddle of mud. Anyone standing in the room who 
does anything may slip and fall face-first into the muck, and is left 
sitting: a good moment to strike, or to get away. Nimble feet 
(dexterity) help to keep your balance. Careful: the caster can slip too.
</p><p>The puddle dries up after its first victim falls, or by itself after a 
minute or so, longer the better it was cast.
</p><p>It can't be cast indoors, in the desert, on water or in a swamp, or on 
snow, slush or ice. You must be standing. It is also found on scrolls, 
wands and staffs.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
